<%# The shop words that no mapping answers yet, biggest first.

    One decision here classifies every candidate that carries the word, in this
    run and in every later one. In the first full run the two hundred biggest
    pairs covered 45% of all candidates, which makes this page the cheapest hour
    of the whole import.

    A word can also be refused. "Vinyl" and "Merch" are decisions too, and are
    made one time rather than once per run. %>

<div class="mb-8">
  <h2 class="font-bold text-xl mb-2">Shop categories with no mapping</h2>

  <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-4">
    Each row is one decision. It applies to every candidate that carries the
    word &mdash; in this run and in every later one &mdash; so the largest rows
    are worth the most. Choose what this catalogue calls it, or say that it
    names nothing this catalogue holds.
  </p>

  <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-4">
    Hold ctrl or cmd to choose more than one: a word can name two things, and
    so can a product. A decision made for <b>any brand</b> answers the word
    wherever it appears.
    A decision made for one brand wins over it, for the shop that means
    something of its own by the same word. After deciding, run
    <code>rake import:map</code> to apply the decisions.
  </p>

  <% if @pairs.empty? %>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
      Every shop category that candidates carry has a mapping. Candidates
      without a sub category now state no category at all, and have to be
      classified by their name.
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="text-sm w-full">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th class="text-left pr-4 pb-2">Brand</th>
            <th class="text-left pr-4 pb-2">The shop says</th>
            <th class="text-right pr-4 pb-2">Candidates</th>
            <th class="text-left pb-2">This catalogue calls it</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% @pairs.each do |(brand_id, word), count| %>
            <tr class="border-t border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">
              <td class="pr-4 py-2 whitespace-nowrap">
                <%= brand_id ? (@brands[brand_id]&.name || brand_id) : 'any brand' %>
              </td>
              <td class="pr-4 py-2 font-bold"><%= word %></td>
              <td class="pr-4 py-2 text-right"><%= count %></td>
              <td class="py-2">
                <%= form_tag admin_import_category_mappings_path, method: :post,
                             class: 'flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2' do %>
                  <%= hidden_field_tag 'import_category_mapping[brand_id]', brand_id %>
                  <%= hidden_field_tag 'import_category_mapping[source_category]', word %>
                  <%# More than one may be chosen: a word can name two things,
                      and a product can be two things. %>
                  <%= select_tag 'import_category_mapping[sub_category_ids][]',
                        options_from_collection_for_select(@sub_categories, :id, :name),
                        multiple: true, size: 4, class: 'text-sm' %>
                  <label class="text-sm whitespace-nowrap">
                    <%= check_box_tag 'import_category_mapping[out_of_scope]', '1' %>
                    not a product here
                  </label>
                  <%= submit_tag 'Save', class: 'cursor-pointer' %>
                <% end %>
              </td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
